{"key":"enterprise/T1055.002","id":"T1055.002","name":"Portable Executable Injection","domain":"enterprise","level":"subtechnique","parent_id":"T1055","tactics":["privilege-escalation","stealth"],"platforms":["Windows"],"environments":["cloud-hosted-endpoint","onprem"],"environment_basis":"project_taxonomy_from_upstream_platforms","summary":"Adversaries may inject portable executables (PE) into processes in order to evade process-based defenses as well as possibly elevate privileges. PE injection is a method of executing arbitrary code in the address space of a separate live process. PE injection is commonly performed by copying code (perhaps without a file on disk) into the virtual address space of the target process before invoking it via a new thread. The write can be performed…","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1055/002","source_stix_id":"attack-pattern--806a49c4-970d-43f9-9acc-ac0ee11e6662","source_modified":"2026-05-12T15:12:00.665Z","source_object_version":"2.0","telemetry":{"status":"mapped","components":[{"id":"DC0039","name":"File Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0039","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--2b3bfe19-d59a-460d-93bb-2f546adc2d2c","page":"telemetry/DC0039/"},{"id":"DC0035","name":"Process Access","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0035","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--1887a270-576a-4049-84de-ef746b2572d6","page":"telemetry/DC0035/"},{"id":"DC0032","name":"Process Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0032","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3d20385b-24ef-40e1-9f56-f39750379077","page":"telemetry/DC0032/"},{"id":"DC0020","name":"Process Modification","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0020","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--d5fca4e4-e47a-487b-873f-3d22f8865e96","page":"telemetry/DC0020/"}],"strategies":[{"id":"DET0106","name":"Behavioral Detection of PE Injection via Remote Memory Mapping","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0106","s